A `frontmatter-update` hook carrying only key=value pairs writes them onto the run artifact itself.
Its report line has no target prefix, and it follows the status line the edge always sets first.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-hooks
title: Hooks
summary: Hook-bearing fixture for playbook-transition.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  only: []

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: noted
            when: the keys are recorded
            hooks: ["frontmatter-update noted=recorded reviewer=alpha"]
      noted: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-hooks/only/prompt.md --
---
summary: Only step.
---

Only body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/.keep --
-- cmd --
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks intaking --workdir run
booping playbook-transition fx-hooks noted --workdir run
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
created index.md
not-started → intaking
frontmatter: status=intaking
intaking → noted
frontmatter: status=noted
frontmatter: noted=recorded reviewer=alpha
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/run/index.md --
---
status: noted
noted: recorded
reviewer: alpha
---
